# What must NOT go into the release zip.
#
# One list, honoured by `build-release.php` and by `wp dist-archive` if you use WP-CLI, so the
# two can never disagree about what ships.
#
# The rule applied here: a file ships if a SITE needs it at runtime. Everything that only a
# developer needs stays behind. Excluding a needed file breaks the plugin; including an
# unneeded one bloats the download and, for the dev docs below, publishes notes that were
# never written for an audience.

# --- Version control / editor -----------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.distignore
.vscode
.idea

# --- Build tooling ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# `tools/` is the 39 MB Tailwind standalone binary. `tailwind.config.js` only matters when
# rebuilding the CSS, which is done before packaging, never on a site.
tools
tailwind.config.js
build-release.php

# --- Tests ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ~460 KB of suites and harnesses. They stub WordPress rather than loading it, so they are
# useless on a real install, and they would be the only PHP in the zip that is not part of the
# plugin.
tests

# --- Developer documentation ------------------------------------------------
#
# DESIGN.md is the design system and build instructions. PLUGIN-CONTEXT.md holds naming
# research, competitor notes and internal decisions — it was written for the team, not for
# users, and it must not be published. SPRINT-PLAN.txt is a worklog.
#
# SECURITY.md deliberately DOES ship: readme.txt points users at it, and it is the honest
# record of what was audited. Everything in it is derivable from the PHP source, which ships
# anyway, so it discloses nothing new.
DESIGN.md
PLUGIN-CONTEXT.md
SPRINT-PLAN.txt

# --- Dependency manifest ----------------------------------------------------
#
# The autoloader is hand-rolled and there is no `vendor/`, so composer.json serves local
# tooling only. Nothing on a site reads it.
composer.json
composer.lock
vendor
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json

# --- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
*.zip

# --- Noise ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.sql
*.bak
*.orig
*~
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
._*
